From d93a8acc7c1279bc9a541b273ce88a0bab24f351 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LiBr <me@nvme0n1p.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:48:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/57] Z 6III: ../z9-qemu's capture models, revision deb3a75

../z9-qemu moved from 2749873 to deb3a75 ("Implement full RAW capture,
virtual card writing and post-shot recovery"): the Z 9's shutter path end
to end -- full-frame Bayer transport through the primary d980 unit, packed
14-bit RAW output, NV16 conversion and thumbnails, the 15e2 JPEG encoder
(libjpeg), CCOMP/capture GPIO handshakes, a DesignWare PCIe adapter onto
QEMU's NVMe for the CFexpress card -- and a later revision of the live
view models: completions after the RAW-derived writes for MIPU_LV (0x1514)
and FRECT_LV (0x151c), a stopped-source reset profile that gates new
pixel work on the source clock, secondary timing, source boundaries. The
new models are opt-in, as there; the Z 6III's switch list gains only
raw-pipeline-1514-completion-model.

import_z9lab.py takes the new board file and copies every model header
(nikon-z9-capture-nv16.h, -d980.h, -jpeg.h, -thumbnail-nv16.h, -pcie.h
are new). Its edits 1-6 apply unchanged; edit 7, the live-view edits,
follows the code that moved: the frame clock's update now also cancels a
prepared d980 single frame, its tick also drives the source boundary and
the d980 stream, +0x210's W1C admits the d980 and 150d bits, FRECT's gate
also starts or cancels the capture NV16 path, engine 0x1542's writes feed
the RAM input. MIPU_LV's bit 3 after a frame is now ../z9-qemu's own
raw-pipeline-1514-completion-model -- it found the same completion in the
ZR image (40e0db5c -> 40eac290 -> event 410b0002), and this image's
lane 0 waits for it the same way (sub_40C0D7C4 -> 0x410b0002 ->
sub_40E6DEC8) -- in place of this board's copy; it also holds the next
frame until the firmware has acknowledged it.

The build links libjpeg for the JPEG encoder (hw/arm/meson.build); the
DesignWare host and NVMe are already in the aarch64 device set. The
capture path itself is not attached yet: no card, no PCIe window, the
capture switches off.

Verified: same live view as before the import (frame jobs complete, MENU
opens over live view, no camera error). smoke.sh passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
